The Vite development server receives it and returns client/index.html.
The browser reads the script tag and loads client/src/main.tsx.
React initializes: ReactDOM.createRoot is called, creating the React tree.
The <App /> component executes (client/src/App.tsx).
The <BrowserRouter> initializes.
The <Routes> component evaluates the current path (/).
The route <Route path="/" element={<LoginPage />} /> matches.
