PART 8 — SERVER REQUEST TIMELINE
When a voter enters their Voter ID on the EVM and clicks "Verify & Send OTP", here is the exact full-stack chain:

React component: VerifyScreen inside VotingMachinePage.tsx ↓ Event Handler: handleSubmit executes. ↓ Service function: votingService.initiateVerification(data) in client/src/services/api.service.ts ↓ HTTP request: Axios sends a POST request to /api/voting/verify/initiate. ↓ Server port: Express receives the request on port 5000. ↓ Middleware (Global): app.ts runs cors(), express.json(), etc. ↓ Route: voting.routes.ts matches /verify/initiate. ↓ Middleware (Route-specific): validate(voterVerificationSchema) validates the payload. ↓ Controller: VotingController.initiateVerification inside voting.controller.ts. ↓ Service: verificationService.initiateVerification (handles business logic). ↓ Prisma/ORM: Prisma translates the query to SQL (prisma.voter.findUnique). ↓ MySQL: The database finds the voter and returns the record. ↓ Server response: sendSuccess(res, result) sends a 200 OK JSON response. ↓ Client: Axios resolves the Promise in the React component. ↓ State update: onVerified(result) is called, triggering setScreen('otp'). ↓ UI: The VerifyScreen unmounts, and the OTPScreen renders.

