PART 10 — DATABASE CONNECTION
When you open http://localhost:5173/ or http://localhost:5173/voting-machine, the browser NEVER directly connects to MySQL.

Modern web architecture strictly isolates the database from the client for security.

The Actual Architecture:

Browser (React Client): Runs on the user's computer. It cannot talk to MySQL. It can only make HTTP requests.
Server (Express API): Runs in a secure environment. It receives HTTP requests from the client.
Database (MySQL via Prisma): Only the Express server has the credentials (in .env) and the Prisma library to talk to the database over TCP.
Execution flow: Browser (axios) ──(HTTP/JSON)──> Server (Express) ──(TCP/SQL)──> Database (MySQL)

If a page (like /) does not make an API request, the server and database are completely untouched during page load.

