PART 12 — SIMPLE EXPLANATION FOR MY PROFESSOR
"When I start the project, two isolated systems come online: Vite serves our React frontend, and Express powers our backend API connected to MySQL via Prisma. When I open localhost:5173, the browser requests the HTML, which pulls in our React code. The root App.tsx file acts as a traffic director using React Router. When it sees the /voting-machine URL, it immediately renders the VotingMachinePage component.

At this exact moment, no database queries happen. The UI is completely static. It only springs into action when a user enters their Voter ID and clicks verify. At that moment, the React component uses Axios to send a POST request to our Express server. The server routes that request to a controller, which asks Prisma to check MySQL for the voter's credentials. The server responds with success, React updates its internal state, and the UI smoothly transitions to the OTP screen."